> ---
> 
> # `ConversationMemory`
> 
> This object persists for one conversation and is responsible for:
> 
> - storing the transcript as it unfolds
> - updating running state
> - generating the prompt-ready memory text
> - producing a final summary if needed
> - exposing the final transcript for `LongTermMemory.post_process_conversation`
> 
> ```python
> class ConversationMemory:
>     def __init__(
>         self,
>         user_id: str,
>         conversation_id: str,
>         long_term_memory: LongTermMemory,
>         initial_retrieved_bundle: Optional[RetrievedMemoryBundle] = None,
>     ) -> None:
>         self.user_id = user_id
>         self.conversation_id = conversation_id
>         self.long_term_memory = long_term_memory
> 
>         now = datetime.utcnow()
>         self.transcript = ConversationTranscript(
>             conversation_id=conversation_id,
>             user_id=user_id,
>             started_at=now,
>             ended_at=None,
>             messages=[],
>             metadata={},
>         )
> 
>         self.state = ConversationState(
>             conversation_id=conversation_id,
>             user_id=user_id,
>             running_summary="",
>             last_updated=now,
>         )
> 
>         self.initial_retrieved_bundle = initial_retrieved_bundle
>         self._latest_memory_block: str = (
>             initial_retrieved_bundle.generated_summary_block
>             if initial_retrieved_bundle is not None
>             else ""
>         )
> ```
